16. Difference Between orElse() and orElseGet()

Input:

Optional.of("Java")

Code:

Optional.of("Java")
        .orElse(getValue());

Output:

Java

Explanation:
getValue() executes even though Optional contains a value.

-------------------------

Code:

Optional.of("Java")
        .orElseGet(() -> getValue());

Output:

Java

Explanation:
getValue() executes only when value is absent.

